  "notes_for_editor": "Pre-1895 official reports are not in the corpus, so the 1842 Hopkins statement, Captain Smith's letter and the 1896 Scribner's passage are cited second-hand through D'Entremont (New England Lighthouses), and the 1933 gale report through LighthouseFriends (the 1933 Courier-Gazette itself not read). Dates from LighthouseFriends only (11 Jan 1908, 1927 ducks, 1946 and 1950 Coast Guard episodes, 1960 demolition, 2009 excess offer, 1914 lens) are single-source. D'Entremont dates the Orcutt/Bowden revolver incident 1874 but the USLHS roster has Bowden as an assistant only from 1880: flagged in the story. Tower height differs by source. Roster: 104 lines from USLHS, copied as printed; USCG lines given role crew; no roster names matched across stations. NRHP 'Mount Desert' is the Mount Desert Rock/Light tower per nomination wording. The 1883 lantern date (NRHP) and the 1855 lantern (LF) both given. Current optic (2017 solar LED) from USLHS place record; not independently checked against the Light List. Wikipedia read for leads only. Fact-check: D'Entremont dates the Nov-Dec storm episode 1951 (tug Snohomish) vs LighthouseFriends 1950 (icebreaker); both stated in story. Hopkins statement: LF says 1842, D'Entremont says Lewis's 1843 report; both stated.",
